{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:InformationTheory.VanDerWaalsHopfChannel","@type":"LeanModule","name":"InformationTheory.VanDerWaalsHopfChannel","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Units.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Invertible.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VanDerWaals.vdw_idempotent_cleared","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VanDerWaals.vdw_idempotent_cleared","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/van-der-waals-hopf-channel.lean#L67-L81","doc":"**The van der Waals block is idempotent** (cleared form): given the Hecke\nrelation `σ² = (q − q⁻¹)σ + 1`, `(σ + q⁻¹)² = (σ + q⁻¹)(q + q⁻¹)`, i.e.\n`e₊² = e₊` after dividing by `(q + q⁻¹)²` — the algebraic signature of a\ngenuine Wedderburn projector.\n\nIn this cleared form nothing is divided at all: the identity is a\n`linear_combination` of the Hecke relation and the unit relation\n`q⁻¹ · q = 1`, so `[2]_q` need not be invertible here. Sorry-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VanDerWaals.blocks_partition_unity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VanDerWaals.blocks_partition_unity","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/van-der-waals-hopf-channel.lean#L56-L65","doc":"The two blocks partition unity: `e₊ + e₋ = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VanDerWaals.directionalBlock","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VanDerWaals.directionalBlock","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/van-der-waals-hopf-channel.lean#L50-L54","doc":"The complementary **directional (hydrogen-bond) block**\n`e₋ = (q − σ)·⅟[2]_q` (antisymmetric / sign rep). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VanDerWaals.vdwSymmetricBlock","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VanDerWaals.vdwSymmetricBlock","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/van-der-waals-hopf-channel.lean#L43-L48","doc":"**Van der Waals channel** — the symmetric-block idempotent\n`e₊ = (σ + q⁻¹)·⅟[2]_q` of the inter-molecular `H_2(q)` (the Hopf /\n`[2]_q` block, `Vol = 0`). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:van-der-waals-hopf-channel","label":"def:van-der-waals-hopf-channel","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/van-der-waals-hopf-channel.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}